                "metadata": {
                    "note": "Marketplace",
                    "author": "Tender Tales",
                    "seriestitle": "Fifth Collection",
                    "category": "stories",
                    "seriesorder": "5",
                    "description": "A boy feels left out when he isn’t invited to a birthday party. Two siblings argue during the drive to a fall fair. A child is teased at school during recess.  Blending seriousness with silliness, these stories gently explore the real-life ups and downs of being a kid. They focus on themes including friendship dynamics, sibling conflicts, anxiety, gratitude, and bullying. As children see themselves in Tender Tales characters, they develop empathy, resilience, and a sense of humor to navigate everyday struggles. Tender Tales are inclusive stories that value all children and families 🏳️‍🌈.",
